.git
.venv
.venv-actor
# NOTHING THAT BUILDS FROM THIS CONTEXT NEEDS THESE, and they are most of it.
#
# `control/images/Dockerfile.pyworker` is the only Dockerfile whose context is the repo root — `kontra
# deploy` tars it to build `kontra-host:1` — and it COPYs `sdk/python` + `runtime/python` and
# nothing else. Without
# these two lines that build streams ~1.5 GB to the daemon before the first RUN: 500 MB of
# orchestrator dependencies and a scratch directory full of transcripts. On a box where disk is
# the thing that runs out, an ignored file is cheaper than a deleted one.
**/node_modules
.scratch
.demo
*.jsonl
.pytest_cache
__pycache__
*.pyc
*.egg-info
build
dist
out
sdk/python/kontra/v1
# the example actors live in the seam but are NOT runtime — keep them out of the
# kontra-host base (its build context is the repo root; the per-actor images build
# from their own context under examples/python/<name>, unaffected by this).
# The CLI image still needs the seeded hello actor (ADR 0047).
examples/python
!examples/python/hello

# Compiled example binaries — 52 MB each, and .gitignore does NOT apply to Docker: a Go
# actor's build context is the repo root (it needs sdk/go + runtime/go), so every sibling example's
# binary rode along. That is what filled the disk mid-deploy. Listed explicitly because
# Docker's matcher cannot express .gitignore's "no extension" shape rule — so a NEW example
# needs a line here. The examples' SOURCES must stay: the actor being built lives among them.
examples/go/subfinder/subfinder
examples/go/nuclei/nuclei
examples/go/desync/desync
examples/go/dnsfacts/dnsfacts
examples/go/linkfind/linkfind
